<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis — Code-to-model traceability: 64/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Functions have concise docstrings (L37-130), but do not map code blocks to numbered equations in Menshykau & Iber (2013) Eqs. (1)-(7), Zubkov et al. (2015), Watanabe & Costantini (2004) Table 1, Basson et al. (2005), or the 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_054_kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L37–L142: Brief docstrings without equation-level or Lean 4 theorem cross-references <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L37-L142>" ;
    pk:hasScore 6.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Evaluates the homogeneous steady state (R*, G*), Jacobian entries, and linearized Turing dispersion relation Re(sigma(k)) (L37-94), and runs a 1D explicit Euler reaction-diffusion solver on an isolated arc (L97-125). However, the ureteric tree in `build_symmetric_ureteric_tree` (L128-142) is a hardcoded geometric binary recursion rather than a self-avoiding tree coupled to a 2D mesenchymal GDNF diffusion-consumption PDE field; moreover, tip-splitting mode transitions (elongation m=1 vs dichotomous m=2 vs trichotomous m=3 as a function of rho_tip = pi*R_tip/lambda_c) and genetic/bead perturbations (Spry1-/-, Gdnf+/-, exogenous GDNF bead) are absent." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L128–L142: Uncoupled geometric binary tree lacking 2D mesenchymal GDNF consumption sink and self-avoidance <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L128-L142>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 48/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L198-209) reports only 3 scalar steady-state values (R_star_wt, G_star_wt, lambda_c_wt) without statistical dispersion metrics (RMSE, Pearson r, CV), without comparison to Watanabe & Costantini (2004) E11.0-E13.5 branching generation tip counts and branch angles, and without perturbation deltas for Spry1-/- hyper-branching, GDNF bead ectopic budding, or Gdnf+/- / PRR^(UB-/-) hypoplasia." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L198–L209: Only 3 algebraic steady-state scalars without E11.0-E13.5 generation RMSE/r or perturbation controls <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L198-L209>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-critical-turing-wavelength-lambda-c-at-wild-type-parameters>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-wild-type-homogeneous-steady-state-gdnf-ligand-g>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-wild-type-homogeneous-steady-state-ret-receptor-r> ;
    pk:hasScore 4.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 47.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1 baseline) evaluation of `2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py` (52.4/100). The v1 script computes the homogeneous steady state (R*, G*) = (a + b, b / (a + b)^2) and linearized Turing dispersion curve of the Menshykau & Iber (2013) Schnakenberg-type GDNF-RET reaction-diffusion system, integrates a 1D ampulla arc profile, and draws a purely geometric symmetric binary tree. However, v1 omits dichotomous vs trichotomous tip-splitting mode selection across normalized tip radius R_tip / lambda_c, omits 2D self-avoiding ureteric tree growth driven by local mesenchymal GDNF consumption sinks (-gamma R^2 G), omits Spry1-/- hyper-branching, exogenous GDNF bead supernumerary budding, and Gdnf+/- or PRR^(UB-/-) hypoplasia controls, neither loads nor verifies `datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json`, and performs zero biological specimen segmentation on `datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg`. Overall 47.8/100 (faithfulness 41.0, reproducibility 63.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 58, Morphological realism / specimen match 22, Parameter expressivity 44, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 58, Code-to-model traceability 64, Reproducibility package 68. Output judged: docs/media/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py at 8871db0, image/png, 134295 B, 1890×616 px, artifact_sha256 b5e314ac269c2f687641e61f84f770113eafd6fd8b1ca184f99bb3e0769aabe8 (sha256 b5e314ac269c2f687641e61f84f770113eafd6fd8b1ca184f99bb3e0769aabe8), spec_fingerprint 98ff66f09006e3949d0b868aa475a2ba217b732f0d29cc82d9a5d3b4965aeb50. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 98ff66f09006e3949d0b868aa475a2ba217b732f0d29cc82d9a5d3b4965aeb50; artifact_sha256: b5e314ac269c2f687641e61f84f770113eafd6fd8b1ca184f99bb3e0769aabe8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json=89257794ab9d8d23..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg=3264f509ba3a6686..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/paper_citations.bib=bb8e3d5a5c8877bd..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/scout_manifest.json=c55304eda64bfba4...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Expand `--self-test`, CLI parameter flags (`--a-ret`, `--b-gdnf`, `--gamma`, `--d-ratio`, `--generations`, `--seed`), and `measure_morphoeval()` to report >= 8 quantitative metrics with reference values, dispersion (RMSE, Pearson r, CV), and negative-control ablation deltas.",
        "remediation needed: Implement a 2D self-avoiding ureteric tree branching simulator coupled to a 2D mesenchymal GDNF diffusion-consumption PDE field (where growing tips consume local GDNF via -gamma*R^2*G and steer up-gradient while mutually repelling via GDNF sink depletion), and simulate all 4 experimental regimes: Wild-Type control, Gdnf+/- or PRR^(UB-/-) hypoplasia, Spry1-/- hyper-branching (Basson et al. 2005), and exogenous GDNF-soaked bead ectopic budding.",
        "remediation needed: Implement semi-implicit (IMEX) Schnakenberg GDNF-RET reaction-diffusion solver across ureteric bud ampulla radii R_tip to demonstrate the exact transition from single-peak elongation (rho_tip < 1.5) to canonical dichotomous tip splitting (1.5 <= rho_tip < 2.5, m = 2 lateral R^2*G hotspots with apical cleft) and trichotomous trifurcation (rho_tip >= 2.5, m = 3 hotspots).",
        "remediation needed: Load and SHA-256-verify `datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json` and `kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg` at runtime, segment the E12.5 mouse metanephros whole-mount GFP ureteric bud trees in Panel A (wild-type control, 12 tips) and Panel B (hypoplastic mutant, 6 tips) plus pErk1/2 immunofluorescence intensity in Panels D-I, and extract medial-axis skeleton length, terminal tip counts, and WT-to-mutant tip ratio." ;
    pk:hasScore 4.78e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 44/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
